.TH CGC 1 "2026-11-10" "cgc 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cgc \- clone, fetch, pull, and update Git repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cgc
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIREPOSITORY\fR [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.br
.B cgc fetch
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.br
.B cgc pull
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.br
.B cgc update
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cgc
is a self-contained implementation of
.BR git-clone (1)
that speaks the Git smart HTTP protocol (version 2) directly, and can also read
a local repository without invoking
.BR git (1).
It downloads or copies objects, verifies and unpacks packfiles, resolves deltas,
writes loose objects, refs and configuration, and checks out the working tree
with a Git-compatible index.
.PP
The
.BR fetch ,
.B pull
and
.B update
subcommands update an existing clone.
.B fetch
downloads missing objects and updates remote-tracking refs and tags.
.B pull
(and its alias
.BR update )
also fast-forwards the current branch and updates the working tree.
.PP
If
.I DIRECTORY
is omitted for a clone, the directory name is derived from the repository name,
with any trailing
.B .git
removed. For subcommands it defaults to the current directory, and parent
directories are searched for the repository.
.SH "REPOSITORY FORMS"
.TP
.B https://\fIhost\fR/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR[.git]
An explicit URL. Plain
.B http://
is accepted for local testing.
.TP
.B \fI/path/to/repo\fR
A local repository: a working tree with a
.B .git
directory or
.B .git
file (linked worktree), or a bare repository. Relative paths, paths starting
with
.BR ~ ,
and
.B file://
URLs are also accepted. Local repositories are read directly; objects and
packed objects are copied into the destination.
.TP
.B gh:\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://github.com/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
.TP
.B gl:\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://gitlab.com/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
.TP
.B bb:\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://bitbucket.org/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
.TP
.B sym:\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://git.symlinx.net/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
.TP
.B \fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://\fIdefault-host\fR/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
The default host is
.B github.com
and can be changed with
.B \-\-host
or
.BR CGC_DEFAULT_HOST .
.TP
.B \fIhost.tld\fR/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://\fIhost.tld\fR/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B fetch
Fetch missing objects and update
.B refs/remotes/\fIremote\fR/*
and tags, where
.I remote
is the first remote configured in the repository (usually
.BR origin ).
Local branches and the working tree are left untouched.
.B .git/FETCH_HEAD
records what was fetched. In a bare repository,
.B fetch
writes only
.B FETCH_HEAD
and leaves refs unchanged, matching Git's default without a fetch refspec.
When the remote is a local path or
.B file://
URL, objects are copied directly from the source repository, including
unpacking source packfiles. Local transfers copy all objects rather than
negotiating
.B have
lines.
.TP
.B pull
Fetch, then fast-forward the current branch and update the working tree and
index. Refuses to run when the remote branch is not a descendant of the local
branch, when an affected file has local modifications, or when an untracked
path would be overwritten. Staged changes on paths the update does not touch
are preserved; a staged change to an affected path is refused unless it already
matches the new tree.
.B .git/ORIG_HEAD
records the previous
.B HEAD
before it moves.
.TP
.B update
Alias for
.BR pull .
.B pull
is refused in a bare repository because there is no working tree.
.PP
For all subcommands,
.I DIRECTORY
defaults to the current directory and parent directories are searched for the
repository.
.B \-\-branch
selects the branch to fetch or pull. Pull refuses to switch away from an
existing branch, but can create and check out a branch when
.B HEAD
is unborn or detached. From a detached
.BR HEAD ,
.B pull
switches to the branch, fast-forwarding it when possible, keeping the local tip
when it is ahead, and refusing when local and remote have diverged.
.PP
Tags are fetched by default. An existing local tag is never overwritten when
the remote tag points at a different object; use
.B \-\-force
to allow that.
.B \-\-no\-tags
skips tags entirely.
.B \-\-prune
deletes remote-tracking refs for branches deleted upstream, including entries
in
.BR packed\-refs ;
it is skipped when
.B \-\-branch
limits the fetch.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-host \fIhost\fR
Use
.I host
as the default host for the
.IR owner/repo
shorthand. Clone only.
.TP
.B \-\-token \fItok\fR
Use
.I tok
as a bearer token for HTTPS authentication. May also be given via the
.B CGC_TOKEN
or
.B GIT_TOKEN
environment variables. Tokens are never written to
.BR .git/config .
.TP
.B \-\-token\-file \fIpath\fR
Read the bearer token from the first line of
.IR path ,
trimming surrounding whitespace. This keeps the token out of the process
argument list. The file is read before the operation starts.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-branch " \fIname\fR"
When cloning, check out
.I name
(a branch or tag) instead of the remote's default branch. Tags are checked
out in detached HEAD state.
When fetching or pulling, limit the operation to
.I name
(tags are still fetched by
.BR fetch ).
.TP
.B \-\-tags
Fetch and update all advertised tags. This is the default. Fetch, pull, and
update only.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tags
Do not fetch or update tags. Valid when cloning and for fetch, pull, and
update. A tag explicitly selected with
.B \-\-branch
is still checked out.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite a local tag that points at a different object than the remote tag.
Without this option such a fetch is refused before any refs are written. This
does not make
.B pull
accept a non-fast-forward update. Fetch, pull, and update only.
.TP
.B \-\-prune
Delete remote-tracking refs under
.B refs/remotes/\fIremote\fR
that the remote no longer advertises, including entries in
.BR packed\-refs .
Skipped when
.B \-\-branch
limits the fetch. Fetch, pull, and update only.
.TP
.B \-\-depth \fIn\fR
Create a shallow clone with history truncated to
.I n
commits. Writes
.B .git/shallow
with the shallow boundary. Implies
.BR \-\-single\-branch .
Rejected for local repositories. Clone only.
.TP
.B \-\-single\-branch
Clone only the history of one branch. Clone only.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-single\-branch
Fetch all branches (the default unless
.B \-\-depth
is given). Clone only.
.TP
.B \-\-bare
Create a bare repository: objects, refs, and configuration are stored directly
in
.I DIRECTORY
with no working tree or index. When
.I DIRECTORY
is omitted, the derived name keeps a
.B .git
suffix. Clone only.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-checkout
Write
.BR HEAD ,
refs, objects, and configuration, but do not create the index or check out the
working tree. Clone only.
.TP
.B \-\-origin \fIname\fR
Use
.I name
for the remote instead of
.BR origin .
The name is used in config sections, branch upstream settings, and
.B refs/remotes/\fIname\fR/*.
Clone only.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress progress messages and status output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat all remaining arguments as positional, even if they begin with a dash.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cgc gh:octocat/Hello-World
cgc sym:team/repo
cgc octocat/Hello-World my-copy
cgc https://github.com/torvalds/linux.git
cgc \-\-host git.example.com team/repo
CGC_DEFAULT_HOST=git.example.com cgc team/repo
cgc \-\-bare gh:owner/repo
cgc \-\-no\-checkout gh:owner/repo
cgc \-\-origin upstream gh:owner/repo
cgc \-\-no\-tags gh:owner/repo
cgc /srv/git/project.git
cgc file:///srv/git/project.git project\-copy
cd repo && cgc fetch
cd repo && cgc pull
cd repo && cgc fetch \-\-prune
cd repo && cgc fetch \-\-no\-tags
cgc pull \-\-branch main /path/to/repo
.fi
.SH OUTPUT
Status is written to standard error in the style of
.BR git-clone (1):
.BR "Cloning into '...'..." ,
any
.B remote:
messages sent by the server, a
.B Receiving objects
download meter,
.BR "Resolving deltas" ,
and
.B Updating files
during checkout.
.B fetch
prints a
.B From
block listing new and updated branches and tags.
.B pull
also prints
.B Updating
and
.BR Fast-forward ,
or
.B Already up to date.
when there is nothing to do.
Live meters are drawn only when standard error is a terminal; final summary
lines are printed when output is redirected.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CGC_DEFAULT_HOST
Default host used for the
.IR owner/repo
shorthand when
.B \-\-host
is not given.
.TP
.B CGC_TOKEN
Bearer token for HTTPS authentication. Used when
.B \-\-token
and
.B \-\-token\-file
are not given.
.TP
.B GIT_TOKEN
Fallback bearer token, used when
.B CGC_TOKEN
is not set.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
The operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
A network, protocol, filesystem, checkout, or fast-forward error occurred.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH SAFETY
The remote repository is treated as untrusted. Ref names and
.B HEAD
targets supplied by the server are validated before use, configuration values
are rejected if they contain control characters, and checkout refuses duplicate
paths, file/directory collisions, and paths whose existing parent is a symlink.
This prevents a malicious repository from writing outside the target directory.
.PP
.B pull
checks the working tree before changing it: an affected file must still match
the old commit, and an added path must not already exist as an untracked file.
If either check fails, nothing is written. Unrelated staged changes are kept in
the index, including
.B skip\-worktree
and
.B assume\-unchanged
flags. Pull never creates a merge commit or rebases.
.PP
Ref updates are written through a sibling
.B .lock
file and renamed into place.
.BR index ,
.BR FETCH_HEAD ,
and
.B ORIG_HEAD
are written atomically as well, so an interrupted update does not leave a
truncated file behind.
.PP
These checks are not a sandbox: as with
.BR git-clone (1),
do not run code from an untrusted repository without reviewing it.
.SH LIMITATIONS
No SSH or \fBgit://\fR transport; protocol v2 and SHA-1 only; the whole pack and
all inflated objects are held in memory, and a single object larger than 2 GiB
is rejected; local transfers copy every object instead of using
.B have
negotiation, and
.B \-\-depth
is rejected for local repositories; pull is fast-forward-only (no merge, rebase,
or conflict resolution); pull cannot fetch into a shallow clone, cannot run in a
bare repository, or switch away from an existing branch (from a detached HEAD it
can check out a branch when that is a fast-forward or the local tip is ahead);
.B \-\-prune
is skipped when
.B \-\-branch
limits the fetch; custom refspecs, multiple remotes, and
.B \-\-mirror
are not supported; bare fetch records only
.BR FETCH_HEAD ;
tags are fetched in full rather than Git's
reachability-based auto-follow; submodules are not cloned or updated; no partial
clone, LFS, hooks, or reflogs; no retry or resume on network failures.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR git-clone (1),
.BR git-upload-pack (1),
.BR gitprotocol-v2 (5),
.BR git (1)
